The README's goal example, word for word: a goal said the way a person says
it, with no mention of Gno or mem, only that the work carries on in
another session. The first session must keep the goal in mem and do one
step; a new session, which has only what was kept, must carry on to done.

-- project/go.mod --
module stats

go 1.22
-- project/stats.go --
package stats

// Mean returns the average of xs.
func Mean(xs []int) float64 {
	if len(xs) == 0 {
		return 0
	}
	sum := 0
	for _, x := range xs {
		sum += x
	}
	return float64(sum) / float64(len(xs))
}
-- prompt --
